

17. Cloud Cost, Performance &amp; Capacity Optimization Agent


Create an infrastructure optimization agent that reviews cloud spend, utilization, scaling policies, idle
resources, database performance, container metrics, storage growth, and service-level objectives. The
agent should recommend rightsizing, scheduling, autoscaling, reserved-capacity options, and performance
tuning actions with business-impact explanations. Bonus: propose changes as infrastructure-as-code pull
requests for platform team review.
Objective: Balance technology cost, performance, and resilience by continuously optimizing the cloud and
platform estate.
Learning takeaways: FinOps analytics, capacity planning, SLO-based optimization, infrastructure-as-code
generation, cloud telemetry analysis, performance bottleneck detection, and approval-based automation.



